;; unsupported_claims — verified claims with NO source span (REQ-KG-006).
;;
;; Booklogic port of assets/queries/coverage/unsupported_claims.rq:
;;   SELECT ?claim WHERE {
;;     ?claim tbf:status "verified" .
;;     FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?claim prov:wasDerivedFrom ?src . }
;;   }
;;
;; The :where binds the claim id and pins status = "verified". The :not negates
;; a source-span joined on the claim id (the projector populates
;; source-span/claim-id as the back-reference to the owning claim), so this
;; lowers to a safe Cozo negation: "verified claims for which no source-span
;; row shares the claim id". A claim with no provenance is the data-quality gap
;; this query audits.
;;
;; DIVERGENCE FROM THE RDF QUERY — reconcile at P5 cutover. The .rq negates
;; `prov:wasDerivedFrom`, which project_graph emits for BOTH source spans and
;; `derived_from` claim refs. This port negates only the source-span back-ref, so
;; a verified claim whose only provenance is a `derived_from` link would be
;; flagged unsupported by Cozo but not by SPARQL. Bermuda has zero `derived_from`
;; claims, so the goldens coincide; P5 should either project a derived-from edge
;; into the negation or confirm source-span is the intended provenance signal.
(defquery :unsupported-claims
  :find  [?claim]
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?claim]
          [?c :claim/status "verified"]]
  :not   [[?s :source-span/claim-id ?claim]])
